{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqd64xspaoc","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Judge drain pressure nudge should suppress when real work is in flight","summary":"Problem: the /judge/pressure nudge fires unconditionally on every UserPromptSubmit, even when the dispatcher session is actively coordinating real implementation subagents. This causes judge drain batches to run concurrently with real work — token waste and noise.\n\nFix: before issuing a judge agent_id, check if the session has active workers on non-drain tasks (task_key != \"followup/harness-judge-drain\"). If any real workers are in-flight → suppress the nudge (return idle, no agent_id). Only fire the judge nudge when the session is idle: no active real workers, no ready tasks being dispatched.\n\nImplementation: in the /judge/pressure endpoint (or wherever the UserPromptSubmit nudge is generated), query active agents for the session and filter out drain workers. If count > 0 → suppress.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T02:31:59.257Z","vec":[-0.04100698232650757,0.0415397584438324,-0.06018713489174843,0.01752808503806591,-0.008449527435004711,-0.040968816727399826,0.12555986642837524,-0.06168288737535477,0.0016410491662099957,0.03166559711098671,-0.04256420582532883,-0.052869703620672226,-0.061124105006456375,0.03662153705954552,-0.057129956781864166,0.049024101346731186,0.10880903154611588,-0.035116273909807205,-0.005961115937680006,-0.051089800894260406,0.025901824235916138,0.017274050042033195,0.04658807814121246,0.04369733855128288,-0.08817844092845917,-0.03611990809440613,-0.04636600241065025,-0.07882381975650787,0.033773887902498245,-0.07296667248010635,0.0006708978908136487,-0.019036969169974327,-0.055101845413446426,-0.03239016979932785,0.10997859388589859,-0.045344747602939606,0.03355086222290993,0.012040884234011173,0.0026815326418727636,0.0035507027059793472,0.07544337958097458,-0.017159871757030487,-0.05626948922872543,0.03271887078881264,-0.04979905113577843,0.0